.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1055 AM PDT Wed Oct 14 2026

VFR conditions are forecast for much of the region through the
TAF period as high pressure builds in from the eastern Pacific. As
mentioned earlier, some of the high resolution models are showing
stratus developing late tonight and into Thursday morning, yet
mainly along the coast of the North Bay and San Francisco
Peninsula. Onshore winds are forecast to return by early afternoon
and prevail into the early evening before becoming light/variable
and then weak offshore early Thursday morning. Medium to high
confidence for inland and low to moderate for coastal sites.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR. Light/variable to offshore flow this
morning becoming onshore by early afternoon. Winds are forecast to
be west- northwest between 10-15kt before easing after sunset.
Weak offshore flow is forecast after sunrise before becoming
onshore by early Thursday afternoon.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR. Onshore winds have returned to MRY
while drainage (southeasterly) winds persist at SNS. Onshore flow
is expected by early afternoon at both terminals before easing
after sunset.

