.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 502 AM PDT Wed Oct 14 2026

Elevated to near critical fire weather conditions are expected for
the higher elevations late tonight through Friday morning. The main
areas of concern will be for the North Bay Interior Mountains and
East Bay Hills. The strongest winds look to be over the North Bay
Interior Mountains where gusts 30-40 mph are possible, perhaps up to
45mph or higher for the highest elevations. The East Bay Hills will
be breezy as well, but may be closer to 25-35 mph with locally
higher gust for exposed ridges and areas of higher terrain. Both
areas will be dry with poor overnight RH recovery, which combined
with the breezy winds, warmer weather, and available fuels leads to
the elevated to near critical fire weather conditions.

